{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK10OidcPolicyV","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OidcPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"role":"symbol","title":"OidcPolicy","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OidcPolicy","kind":"identifier"}]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"OpenID Connect surface controls (X7 G8, plan §4.6\/§4.8; T21.4). Settings that are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"password rules, here because this is the org-baseline-plus-tenant-override surface every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other per-tenant control lives on. They are not all of the same kind as each other, and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is which is the whole of what ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate_tenant_override"},{"type":"text","text":"] and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clamp_overrides_to_org"},{"type":"text","text":"] read, so it is set out rather than inferred. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ordered","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant may be stricter than its organization and never more permissive: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"], validated "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"disable-only","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — the mirror image of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mfa_enforced"},{"type":"text","text":", because releasing personal data is the less-restrictive direction, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant can turn its organization’s decision off but never on. * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::saml_idp_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validated "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disable-only"}]},{"type":"text","text":" exactly like ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"] (D-20): a tenant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"may turn its organization’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" off and never its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" on. * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::ssf_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validated "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"disable-only","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the same way (D-45). * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dynamic_registration"},{"type":"text","text":"], on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ladder "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"disabled"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"initial_access_token"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymous"},{"type":"text","text":": a tenant may move down it and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never up. * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_max_clients"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_unused_client_ttl_days"},{"type":"text","text":"], on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ordinary "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tenant <= org"},{"type":"text","text":" rule — with the wrinkle that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" on the second means "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"never sweep","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is the longest window of all and is handled by ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_ttl_strictness"},{"type":"text","text":"]. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ordered"}]},{"type":"text","text":", therefore never validated against the baseline and never clamped: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::default_locale"},{"type":"text","text":"]. A language is a presentation preference; there is no sense in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which Italian is stricter than French. * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_allowed_scopes"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::external_client_allowed_resources"},{"type":"text","text":"]. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names per-tenant resources — "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}]},{"type":"text","text":" tenant’s MCP servers, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}]},{"type":"text","text":" tenant’s callback hosts —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and there is no sense in which one such list is stricter than another. A subset rule would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"force an organization to enumerate every tenant’s resource servers in its own baseline"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before any tenant could name one. The model’s rule is “a tenant may only be more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restrictive”, which binds every field that "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"has","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a restrictiveness; a field that has none"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cannot violate it. One cross-field interlock spans both groups and is checked on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resolved policy rather than on either input: see ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate_dcr_policy"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/Se","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SE","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OidcPolicy","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/init(cimd:dcrAllowedRedirectHosts:dcrAllowedScopes:dcrMaxClients:dcrUnusedClientTTLDays:defaultLocale:dynamicRegistration:externalClientAllowedResources:samlIdpEnabled:sensitiveScopesEnabled:ssfEnabled:ssfInactiveReason:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/init(from:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/cimd","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrAllowedRedirectHosts","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrAllowedScopes","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrMaxClients","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrUnusedClientTTLDays","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/defaultLocale","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dynamicRegistration","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/externalClientAllowedResources","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/samlIdpEnabled","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/sensitiveScopesEnabled","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/ssfEnabled","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/ssfInactiveReason"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/encode(to:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods"}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/init(cimd:dcrAllowedRedirectHosts:dcrAllowedScopes:dcrMaxClients:dcrUnusedClientTTLDays:defaultLocale:dynamicRegistration:externalClientAllowedResources:samlIdpEnabled:sensitiveScopesEnabled:ssfEnabled:ssfInactiveReason:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/init(cimd:dcrallowedredirecthosts:dcrallowedscopes:dcrmaxclients:dcrunusedclientttldays:defaultlocale:dynamicregistration:externalclientallowedresources:samlidpenabled:sensitivescopesenabled:ssfenabled:ssfinactivereason:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"cimd","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK10CimdPolicyV","text":"CimdPolicy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrAllowedRedirectHosts","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"]?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"dcrAllowedScopes"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"]?, "},{"text":"dcrMaxClients","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrUnusedClientTTLDays","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultLocale","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dynamicRegistration","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"externalClientAllowedResources","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"samlIdpEnabled","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sensitiveScopesEnabled","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ssfEnabled","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ssfInactiveReason","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/init(cimd:dcrAllowedRedirectHosts:dcrAllowedScopes:dcrMaxClients:dcrUnusedClientTTLDays:defaultLocale:dynamicRegistration:externalClientAllowedResources:samlIdpEnabled:sensitiveScopesEnabled:ssfEnabled:ssfInactiveReason:)","title":"init(cimd:dcrAllowedRedirectHosts:dcrAllowedScopes:dcrMaxClients:dcrUnusedClientTTLDays:defaultLocale:dynamicRegistration:externalClientAllowedResources:samlIdpEnabled:sensitiveScopesEnabled:ssfEnabled:ssfInactiveReason:)","abstract":[]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dcrMaxClients":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dcrmaxclients","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrMaxClients","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrMaxClients","title":"dcrMaxClients","abstract":[{"text":"T21.4 — how many externally registered clients this tenant may hold. See","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DEFAULT_DCR_MAX_CLIENTS"},{"text":"]. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Counted once per mechanism, against the same number"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(T21.8): ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"managed_by: dcr"},{"text":" rows and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"managed_by: cimd"},{"text":" rows each have this many. So a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"tenant running both cannot have shadow rows materialised from documents exhaust the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allowance for self-registration, or the reverse. The CIMD count is checked "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"document is fetched, so a tenant at its ceiling is not an outbound amplifier either. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_"},{"type":"text","text":" name because dynamic registration defined it, on the same precedent as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_allowed_scopes"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dcrAllowedScopes":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"T21.4 — the scopes a self-registered client may ask for. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"scope"},{"type":"text","text":" a registration names"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that is not on this list is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"invalid_client_metadata"},{"type":"text","text":"; an empty list means a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-registered client gets no scopes at all, which is the honest default for a tenant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that has turned registration on without deciding what it grants. May not contain"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"address"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"phone"},{"type":"text","text":" — see this module’s ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sensitive_scope_in_dcr_list"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dcrallowedscopes","title":"dcrAllowedScopes","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrAllowedScopes","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dcrAllowedScopes"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"]?"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dynamicRegistration":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"T21.4 — whether a client may register itself (RFC 7591), and on what terms. ","type":"text"},{"code":"disabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unless somebody says otherwise (I1).","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dynamicRegistration","role":"symbol","title":"dynamicRegistration","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dynamicregistration","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dynamicRegistration"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/init(from:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Decoder","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7DecoderP"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/init(from:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/init(from:)","title":"init(from:)"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/ssfInactiveReason":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Read-only","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", D-55: set on a settings response when "},{"code":"ssf_enabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is on but the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transmitter is inactive anyway, saying why — the deployment holds more than one tenant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and serves no per-tenant issuers. Never stored."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/ssfInactiveReason","role":"symbol","title":"ssfInactiveReason","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/ssfinactivereason","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ssfInactiveReason","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dcrAllowedRedirectHosts":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"T21.4 — hosts a self-registered client’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"redirect_uris"},{"type":"text","text":" may point at, as globs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"*.example.com"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"*"},{"text":" for any). The loopback hosts (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"127.0.0.1"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[::1]"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localhost"},{"type":"text","text":") are always allowed whatever this says, because RFC 8252 §7.3 is how every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"desktop MCP client receives its callback and a tenant that forbade them would have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"turned registration on for nobody."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrAllowedRedirectHosts","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrAllowedRedirectHosts","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dcrallowedredirecthosts","title":"dcrAllowedRedirectHosts"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/ssfEnabled":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"G-5 \/ D-45 — whether the tenant is a Shared Signals Framework transmitter: its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/.well-known\/ssf-configuration"},{"type":"text","text":" is served, its receivers can use the stream management"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API, and events are signed and transmitted on its streams. Default "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Disable-only"}]},{"type":"text","text":", with the shape of ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::saml_idp_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"]: sending security events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"about the organization’s users to third parties is the organization’s decision. Streams"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be registered while it is off; they carry nothing until it is on."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/ssfEnabled","role":"symbol","title":"ssfEnabled","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/ssfenabled","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ssfEnabled"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/externalClientAllowedResources":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"D3"}]},{"text":" — the audiences an externally registered client may address. The single most","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"important field on this policy, and the reason the settings handler refuses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"dynamic_registration: anonymous","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" while it is empty. A client an unrelated party"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registered cannot declare its own "},{"code":"allowed_resources","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; it inherits this list verbatim,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so what a stranger can mint a token "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"for"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is a decision the tenant took in advance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than one the registration request makes. Empty means an externally registered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"client can obtain only today’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axiam:user"},{"type":"text","text":" tokens — which AXIAM’s own APIs accept. That"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is why the interlock exists: the empty list is not a safe default for an "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"open","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registration endpoint, it is the most dangerous one. Shared with T5 (CIMD), which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inherits the same list for the same reason."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/externalClientAllowedResources","role":"symbol","title":"externalClientAllowedResources","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/externalclientallowedresources","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"externalClientAllowedResources"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"]?"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/cimd":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"T21.5 — whether a URL-shaped "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is resolved by fetching the document it names,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and on what terms. See ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CimdPolicy"},{"type":"text","text":"]; off unless somebody turns it on (I1). Nested, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"therefore inherited or overridden "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"whole"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the fields are terms of one decision, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"half-merged posture is one neither the organization nor the tenant wrote."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cimd"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK10CimdPolicyV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"CimdPolicy"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/cimd","title":"cimd","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/cimd"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/sensitiveScopesEnabled":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"address"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"phone"},{"type":"text","text":" may be registered on a client, requested at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authorization endpoint, and released at UserInfo (X7 G8). "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Off unless an organization","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"turns it on.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The two scopes release a postal address and a telephone number —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"categories of personal data AXIAM has no other use for — so the deployment that has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never thought about them releases nothing, and the operator who has thought about them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"says so once, at the organization level, where the lawful basis for holding the data was","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"decided. The switch is a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"capability"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", not a grant: with it on, a client still has to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"register the scope, the request still has to ask for it, and the user still has to have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consented. It is the first of four gates, and it is the only one an operator can close","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for everybody at once.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sensitiveScopesEnabled","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/sensitiveScopesEnabled","title":"sensitiveScopesEnabled","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/sensitivescopesenabled"},"doc://AxiamSDK/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"},"doc://AxiamSDK/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://AxiamSDK/Se":{"title":"Swift.Decodable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/Se"},"doc://AxiamSDK/SE":{"title":"Swift.Encodable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SE"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"title":"AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/samlIdpEnabled":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/samlidpenabled","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"samlIdpEnabled"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/samlIdpEnabled","title":"samlIdpEnabled","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"G-2 \/ D-20 — whether this tenant may act as a SAML 2.0 identity provider: publish IdP"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metadata and accept "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AuthnRequest"},{"type":"text","text":"s on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/saml\/v2\/{tenant}\/{metadata,sso,slo}"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Off"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unless an organization turns it on."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A SAML IdP issues assertions that other systems"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accept as proof of identity, so a deployment that has never decided to be one issues"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none, and the three endpoints answer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"404"},{"type":"text","text":" as if they did not exist. The switch lives on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this policy, beside the other OpenID Provider surface controls, because the SSO endpoint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the same browser login hop and OP session with a different wire format."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Disable-only"}]},{"type":"text","text":", with the shape of ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"]: a tenant may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"turn its organization’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" off but never its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" on, because the decision to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"issue identity assertions on behalf of the organization’s tenants is the organization’s."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A deployment built without the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"saml"},{"type":"text","text":" feature answers "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"404"},{"type":"text","text":" whatever this says; the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"setting is a capability, not a grant (each SP must still be registered, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"allow_idp_initiated"},{"type":"text","text":" is its own opt-in)."}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/defaultLocale":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The BCP 47 tag the sign-in page falls back to when the relying party’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ui_locales"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"selects nothing (W5’s chain, plan §4.6). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"None"},{"type":"text","text":" means “no tenant preference”, which"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lands on the deployment default (","type":"text"},{"code":"en","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") — the behaviour every deployment had before this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field existed. A tag this build does not ship also lands there: the parse is exact","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"rather than a language lookup, so a stored "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fr-CA"},{"type":"text","text":" reads as “somebody wrote something"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this binary does not ship” rather than as a guess at French. Stored as a string rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than as the "},{"code":"Locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" enum because that enum lives in ","type":"text"},{"code":"axiam-oauth2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", four layers above","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this crate, and the crate layering points inward.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultLocale"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"defaultLocale","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/defaultlocale","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/defaultLocale"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/encode(to:)":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/encode(to:)","title":"encode(to:)","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/encode(to:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"encode","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s7EncoderP","text":"Encoder","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dcrUnusedClientTTLDays":{"title":"dcrUnusedClientTTLDays","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrUnusedClientTTLDays","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"T21.4 — how long an externally registered client survives without being used. See"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DEFAULT_DCR_UNUSED_CLIENT_TTL_DAYS"},{"type":"text","text":"]. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" disables the sweep for this tenant, which an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operator who prunes out of band may legitimately want. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two sweeps read it, over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"different clocks","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (T21.8). A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"managed_by: dcr"},{"type":"text","text":" row is measured from its last"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authorization, falling back to when it was registered. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"managed_by: cimd"},{"type":"text","text":" row is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured from the last time its document was "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"presented"}]},{"type":"text","text":", which every authorize, token"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and PAR request moves — so a document in daily use is never swept however old its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registration is, and one nobody has presented since the window is, and re-materialises"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the next request if it is still published. Like the ceiling, it keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name."}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dcrunusedclientttldays","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrUnusedClientTTLDays","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OidcPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OidcPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenID Connect surface controls (X7 G8, plan §4.6\/§4.8; T21.4). Settings that are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"password rules, here because this is the org-baseline-plus-tenant-override surface every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other per-tenant control lives on. They are not all of the same kind as each other, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is which is the whole of what ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate_tenant_override"},{"type":"text","text":"] and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clamp_overrides_to_org"},{"type":"text","text":"] read, so it is set out rather than inferred. "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ordered","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant may be stricter than its organization and never more permissive: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"], validated "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disable-only"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — the mirror image of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mfa_enforced"},{"type":"text","text":", because releasing personal data is the less-restrictive direction, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant can turn its organization’s decision off but never on. * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::saml_idp_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validated "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disable-only"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" exactly like ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"] (D-20): a tenant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"may turn its organization’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" off and never its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" on. * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::ssf_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validated "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"disable-only","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" the same way (D-45). * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dynamic_registration"},{"type":"text","text":"], on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ladder "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"disabled"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"initial_access_token"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymous"},{"type":"text","text":": a tenant may move down it and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never up. * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_max_clients"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_unused_client_ttl_days"},{"type":"text","text":"], on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ordinary "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tenant <= org"},{"type":"text","text":" rule — with the wrinkle that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" on the second means "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"never sweep","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is the longest window of all and is handled by ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_ttl_strictness"},{"type":"text","text":"]. "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ordered"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", therefore never validated against the baseline and never clamped: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::default_locale"},{"type":"text","text":"]. A language is a presentation preference; there is no sense in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which Italian is stricter than French. * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_allowed_scopes"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::external_client_allowed_resources"},{"type":"text","text":"]. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names per-tenant resources — "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" tenant’s MCP servers, "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" tenant’s callback hosts —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and there is no sense in which one such list is stricter than another. A subset rule would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"force an organization to enumerate every tenant’s resource servers in its own baseline"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before any tenant could name one. The model’s rule is “a tenant may only be more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restrictive”, which binds every field that "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"has"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" a restrictiveness; a field that has none"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cannot violate it. One cross-field interlock spans both groups and is checked on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resolved policy rather than on either input: see ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate_dcr_policy"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}],"title":"OidcPolicy"}}}